🛠️ Example CLI Workflows for Multimodal Files

Assuming you have a CLI wrapper for the Gemini API (either a custom script or a community package) installed, here is how you might process the files shown in your mockup:

1. Audio Transcription & Summarization (MP3, WAV)
You can use Gemini 1.5's native audio understanding to transcribe voice memos attached to your notes.
bash
# Appends the transcription directly into your current Obsidian note
geminicli prompt "Please transcribe this audio file and summarize the key action items." --file ./attachments/Interview_Audio.mp3 >> ./Project_Notes.md


2. Image Analysis (PNG, JPEG)
When you attach a design mockup or a whiteboard photo, send it to Gemini for OCR or design critique.
bash
geminicli prompt "Extract all the text from this whiteboard image and format it as a markdown list." --file ./attachments/Design_Mockup.png >> ./Project_Notes.md


3. PDF Document Q&A (PDF)
For long reports, you can attach the file and immediately query it.
bash
geminicli prompt "Read this PDF report and give me a 3-paragraph executive summary." --file ./attachments/Report_Draft.pdf >> ./Project_Notes.md


4. Video Processing (MP4)
Gemini 1.5 Pro can process video frame-by-frame along with the audio track.
bash
geminicli prompt "Watch this video attachment and write step-by-step instructions based on the tutorial." --file ./attachments/Screen_Recording.mp4 >> ./Project_Notes.md


